  × The arguments object doesn't have a map() method.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ function asAny() { (arguments as any).map(() => {}); }
      │                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ function nonNull() { arguments!.map(() => {}); }
    4 │ function typeAssertion() { (<any>arguments).map(() => {}); }
  
  i arguments looks like an array, but it isn't one, so this call throws a TypeError when the code runs.
  
  i Declare a rest parameter, such as ...args, and use it instead, or convert arguments to an array with Array.from(arguments).
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

